bibliograph-mcp - third-party data and services notice

The code in this repository is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE). bibliograph gathers
several source modules that each speak to a different provider's own data or
service, under that provider's own terms. Nothing from these providers is
redistributed by this repository beyond what each source's own README
states; most calls are made live, on request, from the machine running the
server.

  - NDL Search (ndl) and NDL Digital Collections metadata (ndl, dpid
    ndl-dl/ndl-dl-online) - National Diet Library (NDL). Records under the
    declared set are used under NDL's Permission-Free (PDL 1.0) terms,
    compatible with CC BY 4.0. Digital Collections metadata (ndl-dl,
    ndl-dl-online) carries no open licence and is display-only: it is shown
    as returned and not accumulated or redistributed further.

  - NDL Digital Collections full text (ndl_dl) - via NDL Lab
    (lab.ndl.go.jp), National Diet Library. The corpus reached by
    ndl_dl_fulltext_search / ndl_dl_book_fulltext is public domain
    (pre-copyright or copyright-expired holdings digitised under the FY2021
    and FY2022 OCR projects); this server does not accumulate it beyond
    what a tool call returns.

  - NDL Web Archiving Project (WARP, warp) - National Diet Library.
    Archived pages remain the copyright of their original publishers; WARP's
    own terms, not this server's, govern reuse of archived content. See
    docs/sources/warp/README.md, "Terms of use and access".

  - CiNii Research, KAKEN and the NRID researcher directory (cinii) -
    National Institute of Informatics (NII). NRID lookups need a registered
    application id (CINII_APPID); every other CiNii Research call runs
    without one.

  - J-STAGE WebAPI (jstage) - Japan Science and Technology Agency (JST).

  - OpenAlex (openalex) - OurResearch, released under CC0. An OPENALEX_EMAIL
    is recommended (OpenAlex's "polite pool"); OPENALEX_API_KEY is optional.

  - Semantic Scholar Academic Graph API (semantic_scholar) - Allen
    Institute for AI (AI2), under the Semantic Scholar API's own licence
    terms. SEMANTIC_SCHOLAR_API_KEY is optional; keyless calls share one
    throttled pool.

  - Web NDL Authorities (names, name_authority tool) - National Diet
    Library. Catalogue-verified personal-name headings, read live over the
    NDLA SPARQL endpoint.

  - JMnedict, JMdict (English), KANJIDIC2, and KRADFILE/RADKFILE (names),
    all distributed as the `scriptin/jmdict-simplified` JSON release
    (https://github.com/scriptin/jmdict-simplified). These are the property
    of the Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group (EDRDG),
    https://www.edrdg.org/, and are used and redistributable only under the
    EDRDG licence, which requires attribution and share-alike:
    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0),
    https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html

  - Optionally, Wiktionary entries via wiktextract / kaikki.org
    (https://kaikki.org/dictionary/Japanese,
    https://github.com/tatuylonen/wiktextract), for the names source's
    gloss_archaic tool. Wiktionary content is dual CC BY-SA 4.0 / GFDL;
    cite Ylonen, "Wiktextract: Wiktionary as Machine-Readable Structured
    Data", LREC 2022.

bibliograph ships no dictionary or lexical data. Running the names source
requires building a local index with `bibliograph-build-names`
(src/bibliograph/sources/names/build_index.py), which downloads and reshapes the
EDRDG and, optionally, Wiktionary sources listed above. The SQLite index it
produces on your machine carries the same attribution and licence terms as
its sources and is not distributed in, or by, this repository.
